## Context
~/CNRS/code/fs-housekeeper is a git repo on branch main, clean, with an AGENTS.md and no remote. It already has pyproject.toml, uv.lock and a .venv. Its Makefile picks an interpreter with a `PYTHON :=` shell test (.venv/bin/python, else python3) and one recipe uses `uv run --isolated --with black black`; its docs say `pip install -e`. Observed 2026-10-23.

Practice to reach: `rules/coding-python.md` (Environment principles and rules), tracked by 1206.

## Constraints
Closest to aligned: replace the PYTHON detection by the RUN prefix, move black into the dev group of the lock, and rewrite the pip instructions in the docs.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] pyproject.toml and a committed uv.lock describe the dependencies; no hand-kept requirements.txt
- [ ] the Makefile has no PYTHON variable; recipes that run Python tools go through the `RUN` prefix
- [ ] no `pip install` in the Makefile or README
- [ ] the repo's own tests or smoke command pass from a bare shell, output quoted in the PR or log
- [ ] the alignment check of 1206 prints `ok` in ~/CNRS/code/fs-housekeeper
